# A list literal holding `none` is refused where it is written, but `push`
# builds one at run time, and the sentinel `at` answers "not found" with is
# then indistinguishable from an element. `k_index` resolves that the only
# way it can: a demanded read of a stored none is the missing-index err, the
# same answer an out-of-range read gives.
xs = push (push [] 1) none
print "second: {xs[2]!}"
